  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable Integrated D&amp;I systems in Guyana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GGGI is supporting the Government of Guyana to develop concept notes for flood risk management project. During the engagement with the National Drainage and Irrigation Authority (NDIA). NDIA requested GGGI&apos;s support to develop their strategic plan. GGGI has undertaken to add value to the plan&apos;s development by incorporating Nature Based Solutions and climate resilience considerations.This project will therefore support the Government to:1. Examine the potential for integrating Resilience and NbS into Guyana&apos;s drainage and irrigation (D&amp;amp;I) systems2. Develop D&amp;amp;I strategic planning for coastal resilience3. Design a prioritization system for capital works in D&amp;amp;ITogether these interventions are intended to advance and strengthen Guyana&apos;s flood resilience and flood risk management portfolio.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project represents a continuation of the GoG&apos;s efforts in operationalizing a comprehensive flood management solution.</narrative>
  </description>
